@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Setting up an Azure DevOps Organization";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">After creating a Microsoft Azure account, the next step is to set up an Azure DevOps organization. This will allow you to manage repositories, pipelines, and project tracking efficiently.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Step-by-Step Guide to Setting up an Azure DevOps Organization</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to create and configure your Azure DevOps organization:</p>

        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Step 1: Go to Azure DevOps</h4>
                <p>Visit the official Azure DevOps website: <a href="https://dev.azure.com/" target="_blank">dev.azure.com</a> and sign in with your Microsoft account.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-devops-home.png" alt="Azure DevOps Home Page" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure DevOps Home Page</small></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/create-organization.png" alt="Create a new Azure DevOps Organization" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Creating an Azure DevOps Organization</small></p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Step 2: Create a New Organization</h4>
                <p>Click on "Create new organization" and follow the instructions to set up a new DevOps organization. Choose a unique name for your organization.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Step 3: Choose a Region</h4>
                <p>Select the region closest to your team to ensure the best performance. Azure DevOps services will be hosted in this region.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/select-region.png" alt="Select Azure DevOps Region" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Selecting a region for your DevOps Organization</small></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/create-project.png" alt="Create a New Project in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Creating a New Project in Azure DevOps</small></p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Step 4: Create a New Project</h4>
                <p>After creating the organization, create your first project. Choose a name, visibility (public or private), and the version control method (Git or TFVC).</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Setting up an Azure DevOps organization provides a structured way to manage your development projects. With your organization and first project created, you can start working with repositories, pipelines, and boards to streamline your development workflow.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to **navigate the Azure DevOps UI** and explore its various features.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("CreatingAMicrosoftAzureAccount", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Creating a Microsoft Azure Account</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("NavigatingAzureDevOpsUI", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Navigating Azure DevOps UI &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
